    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass. Here's a summary of the redesign.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe `customerCode` is now the region-and-hash identity `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and every value derived from it follows the same identity. Logic is placed by responsibility and existing code is reused rather than copied.\n\n**New/changed units:**\n\n- **`util/Sha256.java`** (new) \u2014 a single home for \"SHA-256 \u2192 first N upper-case hex chars.\" Both identifiers that hash owner fields now use it.\n- **`util/HouseholdIdGenerator.java`** \u2014 refactored to delegate its hex-digest work to `Sha256`, dropping its duplicated `MessageDigest` code.\n- **`model/CustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 owns the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` format: `of(region, telephone, lastName)` builds it (`HASH8` = first 8 upper hex of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`), `regionOf(code)` reads the region back. One class, one responsibility: the code format.\n- **`service/CustomerCodeGenerator.java`** \u2014 now derives the region from the postcode via the existing `Locality` (postcode-preferred, city fallback, `UNKNOWN` default) and delegates formatting to `CustomerCode`. The `OwnerRepository` dependency and the per-city sequence logic are gone \u2014 the code is pure derivation from owner fields.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 `getLocality()` now returns `CustomerCode.regionOf(customerCode)`, so the locality follows the identity instead of being recomputed. `getMembershipNumber()` and `getCheckDigit()` were already built from `customerCode`, so they automatically move to the new identity (javadoc example refreshed).\n- **`OwnerAuditor`** already logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so the create audit record now records the new identity with no change needed (verified in the run: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` field docs/examples to match the new contract.\n\nThe telephone is already normalized to E.164 (`TelephoneNormalizer`) before `saveOwner` generates the code, so `HASH8` hashes the normalized telephone as specified.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
